    <l n="3" type="heading" level="2" para="true">II. <i>Materia hominis generationis</i>
    </l>
    <l n="4" type="heading" level="2">
      <i>est- men eft, compositionis vero corpus orga-</i>
    </l>
    <l n="5" type="heading" level="2">
      <i>nicum vivum sensitivum.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="6" para="true">§.1. Circa hoc theorema explicandæ</l>
    <l n="7">sunt duæ quæstiones, quarum 1. est:</l>
    <l n="8">
      <i>An in homine prater animam rationalem</i>
    </l>
    <l n="9">
      <i>sint quoque anima alia, nempe vegetativa</i>
    </l>
    <l n="10">
      <i>&amp; sensitiva, &amp; 2. An illa anima obti-</i>
    </l>
    <l n="11">
      <i>neant rationem formarum, an rationem</i>
    </l>
    <l n="12">
      <i>materia?</i> Primam quæstionem affir-</l>
    <l n="13">mamus. Quandoquidem enim mate-</l>
    <l n="14">riale &amp; immateriale, corruptibile &amp; in-</l>
    <l n="15">corruptibile, dependens à materia, &amp;</l>
    <l n="16">ab ea independens essentia &amp; proprie-</l>
    <l n="17">tatibus differunt, &amp; vero anima</l>
    <l n="18">vegetativa &amp; sensitiva materiales &amp; corru-</l>
    <l n="19">ptibiles sint, rationalis contra spiri-</l>
    <l n="20">tualis &amp; incorruptibilis, patet, quod</l>
    <l n="21">hæ animæ non possint ulla ratione in</l>
    <l n="22">unam essentiam conjungi, sive id dica-</l>
    <l n="23">tur compositione fieri, sive eminenti</l>
    <l n="24">continentia; quia per eminentem con-</l>
    <l n="25">tinentiam excusari non potest id in spi-</l>
    <l n="26">rituali substantia, quod secundum eam</l>
    <l n="27">rationem qua fit &amp; est, in solidum dependerà</l>
    <l n="28">materia. Accedit deinde, quod</l>
    <l n="29">ab anima rationali anima vegetativa &amp;</l>
    <l n="30">sensitiva realiter sejungi possit,</l>
    <l n="31">ex quo</l>
    <l n="32">evidens</l>
